==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Master A.]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.

==Strategy==
To defeat Master A., send out cats with high health and durability like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] as a meatshield and cats that can tank Master A. like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] as an attacker to chip down Master A. Using some cats with range of over 451 will help greatly, but not [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], as his range is 450.

Despite having less range than Master A., [[Long Distance]] units such as [[Polevaulter Cat]] or [[Medalist Cat]] are able to safely hit Master A. by using the supporting peons as "stepping stones".

[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] is great if you have him. Although it doesn't live long, [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Cat Gang]] can be surprisingly helpful here, damaging Master A. and taking out peons at the same time. Likewise, other [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rushers]] are also helpful.

In case peons keep on absorbing the hits of your cats, you should lure all the peons to your base until the enemy limit has been reached, and until Master A. is near your base. Once the enemy limit of a stage is hit, no more enemies are allowed to spawn until an enemy is killed. After that, kill all the peons before Master A. touches your base, and send out a fast cat such as [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]] to stop him. Mythical Titan Cat can be used to attack him before the inevitable wave of peons catches up to Master A.

